exports[`Unit 20 recorded output: area-circle > matches the authored sample output 1`] = `
"--- area-circle · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   Find the circle's area. Use π = 3.14 and round to the nearest tenth.
display  geometry area-circle diameter 6 unit in name "Circle with diameter 6 in" formulas ["C equals pi times d" row("C = ", "πd"); "A equals pi times r squared" row("A = ", row("π", superscript("r", "2")))]
answer   approx 28.3 ±0.05
input    keypad
keypad   allowDecimal=true
hint     Halve the diameter to get radius, then square it.
step 1   Halve the shown diameter.   [6 ÷ 2 = 3]
step 2   Square the radius.   [3 × 3 = 9]
step 3   Multiply by 3.14.   [3.14 × 9 = 28.26]
step 4   Round to the nearest tenth.   [28.3]
miss     squared-diameter = 113   Square the radius, not the whole diameter.
miss     circumference-for-area = 18.8   Area and circumference use different formulas.

