"--- pythagorean · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   Find the missing side of this right triangle in inches.
display  geometry pythagorean missingSide leg leg 3 hypotenuse 5 unit in name "Right triangle with known leg 3 in, hypotenuse 5 in, and a missing leg" formulas ["c equals the square root of a squared plus b squared" row("c = ", root(row(superscript("a", "2"), " + ", superscript("b", "2")))); "a equals the square root of c squared minus b squared" row("a = ", root(row(superscript("c", "2"), " − ", superscript("b", "2"))))]
answer   exact 4/1
input    keypad
keypad   allowDecimal=true
hint     Subtract the known leg square from the hypotenuse square, then root.
step 1   Square the hypotenuse and known leg.   [5² − 3² = 16]
step 2   Take the square root.   [√16 = 4]
step 3   Use inches for the missing side.   [4 inches]
miss     wrong-hypotenuse-placement = 5.8   Keep the hypotenuse squared alone; subtract the known leg square.
miss     stopped-before-square-root = 16   Take the square root after subtracting the leg square.

