display  geometry pythagorean missingSide leg leg 15 hypotenuse 39 unit m name "Right triangle with known leg 15 m, hypotenuse 39 m, and a missing leg" formulas ["c equals the square root of a squared plus b squared" row("c = ", root(row(superscript("a", "2"), " + ", superscript("b", "2")))); "a equals the square root of c squared minus b squared" row("a = ", root(row(superscript("c", "2"), " − ", superscript("b", "2"))))]
answer   exact 36/1
input    keypad
keypad   allowDecimal=true
hint     Subtract the known leg square from the hypotenuse square, then root.
step 1   Square the hypotenuse and known leg.   [39² − 15² = 1296]
step 2   Take the square root.   [√1296 = 36]
step 3   Use metres for the missing side.   [36 metres]
miss     wrong-hypotenuse-placement = 41.8   Keep the hypotenuse squared alone; subtract the known leg square.
miss     stopped-before-square-root = 1296   Take the square root after subtracting the leg square.

