display  geometry surface-area length 9 width 5 height 14 unit ft faces [length-height, width-height, length-height, width-height, length-width, length-width] name "Rectangular-prism net with length 9 ft, width 5 ft, and height 14 ft" formulas ["SA equals 2lw plus 2lh plus 2wh" row("SA = ", "2lw + 2lh + 2wh"); "V equals l times w times h" row("V = ", "lwh")]
answer   exact 482/1
input    keypad
hint     Add the areas of all six faces in the net.
step 1   Find each pair of face areas.   [45, 126, and 70]
step 2   Double each pair for both faces.   [2(45) + 2(126) + 2(70)]
step 3   Add all six face areas.   [90 + 252 + 140 = 482]
step 4   Use square feet for area.   [482 square feet]

